{"request_sha256": "ee3b1daa94ef4c29d79874ee3cf18e79c1e05982d9060d7a18265a6d245b146f", "prompt_sha256": "847dd718e56258447ec5fcc89fdaadc9701165d02eab0b51001e616ebc1a0329", "dispatched_prompt_sha256": "a17afa7ad5d9230db6815bb0aba41df2f16a1c68648be8744afc63f0e9e3bb37", "schema_sha256": "b11348cd1fb9f87dee1f7d8b64746455da08f64a4885c641943f00ea25a47f5f", "model": "opus", "model_identity_basis": "claude CLI result event modelUsage key: claude-opus-5-5", "effort": "medium", "status": "ok", "forbidden_tools": [], "usage": {"input_tokens": 6, "output_tokens": 8120}, "answer": {"passes": ["pass", "pass", "fail", "fail", "fail", "fail", "pass", "pass", "pass", "pass"], "defects": ["owner-fronds-long-arching (seeds 1 and 42): the crown reads as a palm rosette with arching, drooping lower fronds, but the fronds are still short and have few leaflets compared with reference-0 and reference-1. The crown spread is only about a fifth of the visible trunk height (render-0, render-1). In reference-0 the fronds are a large fraction of the trunk length. About 20-25 fronds are visible, against the inventory's roughly 30-60. The leaflet rows are thin and gappy, where the references show dense, plumose fronds.", "trunk-character (seed 1, P-TRUNK): render-2 shows a smooth, dark trunk with small, sparse, isolated cone-shaped stubs. reference-1 and reference-2 show a trunk fully covered in a spiral diamond lattice of retained leaf bases, with fibre filling the gaps. This is a defining mismatch in what is drawn.", "leaf-base-close (seed 1, P-BASE): render-3 shows a close view of a smooth trunk with about 4 isolated rounded stubs, no lattice and no fibre. reference-2 shows a dense lattice of wedge-shaped leaf bases packed with reddish-brown fibre.", "fruit-clusters-pendent (core in the inventory): the renders have no fruiting bunches. The owner's config records the date cluster (fn-111) as not landed."], "observations": ["render-0 and render-1: a single unbranched trunk with a rosette of pinnate fronds at the top. The newest fronds are held upright and the lowest ones droop below the crown base. The two seeds are closely alike, and render-1 has a slightly curved upper trunk.", "render-2 shows the same seed-1 tree at closer range. The fronds are clearly pinnate, with narrow pointed leaflets, and the lower fronds hang down along the upper trunk. The trunk bows gently and keeps a near-constant diameter.", "The trunk carries no foliage, branches or epiphytes in any render. Its only features are small leaf-base stubs.", "The metadata marks render-3 visibility as 'hidden', but a clear close trunk image was supplied in that position. I assessed the image as shown.", "The finish (flat shading, clean silhouette) is comparable to the spruce anchor-0 at the catalogue floor. The anchor is used for finish quality only, not morphology.", "There is no dead-frond skirt (secondary) and no orange sheath at the crown (secondary). The trunk is straight and upright. That is inside the recorded posture range (trunk-lean-and-curve variation) and is what the owner asks for.", "Epiphytes in reference-1 and reference-2 are variation. Their absence matches the owner's requirement that nothing grows on the trunk."], "findings": [{"observation": "The crown has a palm rosette of pinnate, arching fronds with the lowest drooping below the crown base, in both seeds.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "The fronds are short relative to trunk height, there are fewer of them than in the reference crowns, and the leaflets are sparse and thin. The crown does not yet read as the long, full fronds of reference-0.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Frond length and leaflet size or density dials may still be too low. The owner names these as the first dials."}, {"observation": "The trunk is straight in seed 1 and gently bowed in seed 42, with a near-constant diameter and a slight flare at the base. It is not wavy.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "Nothing grows on the trunk. The only features are leaf-base stubs.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-1"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "The trunk surface is mostly smooth with sparse isolated stubs. It lacks the dense spiral diamond lattice and fibre matting seen in the references.", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-3", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "The trunk organs (fn-110) may be set to low density or small stub size. Fibre fill may not be generated at all."}, {"observation": "There are no pendent fruit clusters. Fruit appears only in reference-0, which is a single specimen, and depends on season and sex. The inventory rates it core, and the owner records fn-111 as not landed.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": "The date cluster organ (fn-111) is not implemented yet."}, {"observation": "Whether leaflets are grouped and set at angles (a V-shaped frond cross-section) cannot be resolved at whole-tree scale. The leaflets are narrow and pointed but look sparse and close to flat.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "required_unknown", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "The finish is at the catalogue floor set by the spruce anchor.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "anchor-0"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}], "coverage": [{"trait_id": "crown-pinnate-arching-fronds", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "explanation": "The rosette shape is supported: pinnate fronds radiate from one point at the top, the new fronds stand upright, and the older ones recurve and droop. Frond count (about 20-25) and length are below the reference crowns, so the owner's long-frond priority fails separately."}, {"trait_id": "leaflet-arrangement-stiff-narrow", "status": "unknown", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "The leaflets are narrow, pointed and bristly-edged, which is consistent. Their grouped insertion and the V-shaped frond cross-section cannot be resolved in the renders, and leaflet density looks much sparser than in the references."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-leaf-base-diamond-pattern", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-3", "reference-1", "reference-2", "reference-0"], "explanation": "The render shows small, sparse, isolated stubs on a smooth trunk. There is no spiral lattice of wedge-shaped leaf bases covering the trunk."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-fibrous-matting", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-3", "render-2", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "The trunk surface is smooth and uniform, with none of the reddish-brown fibre that fills the gaps in the references."}, {"trait_id": "solitary-columnar-stem", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "There is a single unbranched stem of near-constant diameter in both seeds."}, {"trait_id": "fruit-clusters-pendent", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "explanation": "The renders have no fruit bunches. The inventory's core rating rests on one reference, and fruiting depends on season and sex, so this is flagged uncertain. The owner has acknowledged the date cluster (fn-111) as not landed."}]}, "raw_events": "{"type":"system",